{"text": "SANS.\n\nWINE CO.\n\nWINE SPECS\n\n\u00a9 11.5% ABV\ne Fermented with native yeasts\ne Finished unfined & lightly filtered\n\u00a2 Total Acidity: 7.37 g/l\nbd pH: 3.25\ne Free S02: 37 ppm\n\u00a2 Total S02: 60 ppm\ne 205 cases produced\n\nRIESLING\nMCGILL VINEYARD\nRUTHERFORD AVA, 2018\n\nSANS,\n\nRIESLING\n\nMCGILL VINEYARD\n\n|\nRUTHERFORD |\nNAPA VALLEY\n\nThe 2018 Riesling was produced from the McGill Vineyard in the heart of the Rutherford AVA, situated\nbehind Swanson Winery. The 4 acre vineyard is over 60 years old, is not irrigated, and is farmed in house\nby Jake, in a \"beyond organic\" style, without the use of any sprays or herbicides whatsoever. The grapes\nwere hand harvested on September 18, 2018. The grapes went direct to press and then into a chilled\nstainless steel tank where they started and finished fermentation naturally. We racked the wine off of the\nlees prior to filling. Our Riesling finished dry, at 2.2 g/I residual sugar.\n\nThis is one of the few Riesling vineyards remaining in the Napa Valley. Aromas and flavors of lime zest,\nwhite flowers and green apples, finishing with zippy acidity and minerality.\n\nSans Wine Co. is the first producer of premium canned wine in the Napa Valley, founded in 2015 by\nhusband and wife team, Jake Stover and Gina Schober. All wines are produced by Sans Wine (Co.\n\n\"FOR NUNU' is stamped on the bottom of the can, a\nnod to Gina's maternal Grandfather, Al Granzella.\n\"Nunu\" means \u201cGrandpa\u201d In Italian.\n\nWWw.sSanswineco.com\n\ngina@sanswineco.com jake@sanswineco.com",
